<p>A segment of an image tends to seem larger when it&#8217;s filled with visual elements. This is true whether the elements are discrete or continuous.</p>
<p>Above, the right part of the top figure and the left part of the bottom figure each seems to fill more than half of its tier, though plainly these impressions can&#8217;t both be valid.</p>
<p>The illusion was first studied by German physicists Johann Joseph Oppel and August Kundt in the 1860s.</p>
